# Caddy for the production single-node deployment.
#
# This file deliberately declares no site. The Node Agent owns the only HTTP
# server (id "stealth", listening on :443) and rewrites its routes through the
# admin API on every Deploy. Caddy rejects a second server on the same :443
# listener, so the dashboard is not declared here: the Cloudflare Tunnel points
# `console.<domain>` straight at `http://control-plane:3000` and sends every
# Platform Subdomain to `https://caddy:443`.
#
# `local_certs` keeps the certificates Caddy issues internal. The tunnel origin
# is configured with "No TLS Verify" and Cloudflare terminates the public TLS
# session, so Caddy never needs port 80/443 reachable for an ACME challenge.

{
	admin 0.0.0.0:2019
	local_certs
}
